From 605ee2c4fe19591ebbcaa0eae40a433fbfdc41f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:10:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] rhi: vulkan: keep the surface when a window drops to one
 view

With one view again Qt released the swapchain and made the window's
Vulkan surface again, because the Vulkan stereo layer kept its
declaration of a pair for the surface's life, and a one-view swapchain on
that surface was shown as two halves of a pair.

The layer now withdraws its declaration when the surface's pair is no
longer the swapchain presented there (Mesa 26.1.6-1+stereo3d24, ORDER
573), as Mesa's own presentation always did, so the swapchain is built
again on the same surface, naming the old one as oldSwapchain, as for
any other change. Measured on NVIDIA's driver with that layer: a window
that goes from two views to one for good is shown flat (0 pixels differ
between the eyes), two views, one, two ends as the pair, and sixty
changes in six seconds end alive and as the pair, as with the surface
made again; the surface made again cost a new Wayland surface for the
layer and its registry round trip at each change (30 bindings of the
stereo content manager in the sixty changes, 2 without). With the older
layer the window is shown as two halves (244,232 pixels differ), so
libqt6gui6 breaks a layer older than that.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 src/gui/rhi/qrhivulkan.cpp | 9 ---------
 1 file changed, 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gui/rhi/qrhivulkan.cpp b/src/gui/rhi/qrhivulkan.cpp
index 73e65e08..5e4ffc8e 100644
--- a/src/gui/rhi/qrhivulkan.cpp
+++ b/src/gui/rhi/qrhivulkan.cpp
@@ -2678,15 +2678,6 @@ QRhi::FrameOpResult QRhiVulkan::beginFrame(QRhiSwapChain *swapChain, QRhi::Begin
         if (windowWantsTwoViews(swapChainD->window, &platformAnswers) != swapChainD->twoViewsWanted) {
             qCDebug(QRHI_LOG_INFO, "The window now wants %d view(s): building its swapchain again",
                     swapChainD->twoViewsWanted ? 1 : 2);
-            // What was said to the window system about the two views belongs to the surface: a
-            // Vulkan implementation, or a layer over it, may keep its declaration of a pair for
-            // as long as the surface lives, and the one picture would then be shown as the two
-            // halves of a pair. With one view again the surface is therefore made again as well,
-            // after the swapchain that used it is gone.
-            if (swapChainD->stereo && platformAnswers && swapChainD->window->handle()) {
-                releaseSwapChainResources(swapChain);
-                swapChainD->window->handle()->invalidateSurface();
-            }
             if (!swapChainD->createOrResize())
                 return QRhi::FrameOpError;
         }
